{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED: Gerrit 2057 submitted, merged as b46a901937 on main, after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. The first Verified was -1 from tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run, a KNOWN order-dependent flake (open bug de95-1594-1056-436e) provably disjoint from this change; rechecked with that reasoning stated, and the flake itself is being root-caused under its own ticket rather than retried. AC EVIDENCE: 9 acceptance criteria all verified. AC1's command as originally written could never pass - '_CASCADING_EDGES\\\\s*=' does not match a definition that carries a type annotation between the name and the '=', and \\\\s is not basic regex; corrected to 'grep -rnE \"^_CASCADING_EDGES\"', which returns exactly one definition at transition.py:415 with 9 references. All three cascading edges verified by the 32-test suite passing unchanged; the inbound cascade from Gerrit 2044 keeps its own write primitive and topmost-first ordering (7 tests, apply_inbound_events.py untouched - 0 files matched in the landed diff); '* -> closed' still does not cascade; both cascade=False suppression tests pass. reopen was confirmed to already cascade via the (closed -> open) row, answering the open question this ticket posed. Also landed: the review bot's advisory that the unified error message read awkwardly was FIXED rather than deferred - a single verb could not render naturally in both slots ('cannot move to in_progress X', 'its parent could not claim'), so the API now takes an action phrase plus a past participle."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787374729009346001,"uuid":"6b26f6e9-e6e5-4eec-b49b-9e332673b77f"}